WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.802
- There was a Black officer

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.804
who wanted to start
an organization,

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:08.608
an internal organization
where only Black people,

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:12.679 align:start position:0%
and then he would have
preferred only Black gay people

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.280
could come to a meeting, right.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.884 align:start position:0%
So in other words, on government
property inside Langley

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.586
you had to be Black
and you had to be gay

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:21.521
in order to come
to those meetings.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.256 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now, I don't even
know how many people

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:25.425
would fit the bill there,
maybe like seven or eight

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:26.860
so I'm not sure what you'd
have done at that meeting,

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.928
but nevertheless, the point is

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:32.332 align:start size:97% position:3%
there was this very clearly
discriminatory request

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.267 align:start size:88% position:13%
by an officer who should
have known better,

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:37.203
but he made the request and
the Office of General Counsel

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.906
had to come in and say, "No,
that is wildly inappropriate.

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:40.874
We're not doing that."

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.642
And he was actually livid.

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:46.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, he was livid
that he had to be told no

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:48.048
and to be reminded of the law.

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:50.984 align:start size:97% position:3%
So that kind of wokeism
stuff matched with, I think,

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.786
some of the PR stuff you see

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:54.587
coming out of the
CIA these days.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:57.023
You may recall that young
woman in the Twitter video

00:00:57.023 --> 00:01:00.493
saying that she was
a, what was this?

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:04.264
Was it bisexual or lesbian
Latina who has ADHD and-

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:05.498
- Oh, yeah, yeah. She had
a little of everything.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:08.068 align:start size:84% position:16%
- She went through the
woke Olympics list.

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:09.769
So that, I'm sorry to say,

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.805 align:start size:84% position:16%
has really become
the younger culture.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:14.407
And folks who are a little
bit older who came through,

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.509 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think the era,
frankly, of the '90s

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:19.245 align:start size:97% position:3%
such as yourself and myself,
the Gen Xers, we're like,

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:20.613
"Look, we don't
care who you are.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:21.915
Just come in and do the work.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.851 align:start size:84% position:16%
We want to treat
everybody with respect

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.519
and equal opportunity."

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:30.657
But it's now like you now
have to believe what I do.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:33.827 align:start position:0%
And if you don't, you're a
bigot or a racist or homophobic,

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.361
et cetera, and that's new.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's only been in
the past five to 10 years,

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:40.333 align:start size:84% position:16%
really started under
the Obama years.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:43.136
(energetic music)

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:49.075 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I'm Dave Rubin,
and joining me today

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:53.480 line:0%
is a former CIA officer and
host of the new podcast,

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:57.117 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
"The President's Daily
Brief," Bryan Dean Wright.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.551 align:start size:84% position:16%
Welcome back to
"The Rubin Report."

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.920
- Pleasure as always, my friend.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.388
- Bryan, you've been
on a couple times.

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.891 align:start size:84% position:16%
I know you a bit
outside of the show.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.826
I did not know you
were the President.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.828 align:start size:88% position:13%
Is there something
I've been missing here?

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:13.099
- Well, I started first with
a local group of dog owners

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:14.601
as the president of that club

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:17.170
and I've moved all the way to
the White House in my mind.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.005 line:0%
And it's great, just me and Joe

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.974 line:0%
and we're working
on Hunter's laptop.

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:24.644 line:0%
It's gonna be all fixed up.
Don't you worry about that.

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:26.646
- "The President's Daily Brief."

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:27.847
That's the name of the show.

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.916 align:start size:84% position:16%
You have a real
pedigree in the CIA

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:32.051 align:start size:97% position:3%
that I want to talk about
for people that have not seen

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.620 align:start size:88% position:13%
some of your other
appearances on my show.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wanna recap some of that
stuff, but let's just,

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:38.224
just off the name
of the new show,

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.425
"The President's Daily Brief."

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:41.494
Now, I'm not a big
believer in this guy.

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:43.830
Something does not seem
right with this guy.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.733
I'm starting to think this
guy may not be in charge.

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:49.903
Is this your way
of kinda getting in

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:52.839 align:start size:97% position:3%
and in case something happens
saying, "Hey, I'm here,

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:55.141
I've got the title of
the show, et cetera"?

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.610
- I wasn't thinking about that,

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.913
but now that you mention it,
yes, and I'm ready to serve

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.281
because let's be honest,

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:04.784
Kamala is number two and
that's also a hot mess.

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:07.353
And then we got Pelosi. We
all know where that's going.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:10.490
So yeah, it's me. I'm ready.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:11.858
- It's you, it's you.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:14.160
All right, for people
that don't know you,

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.362 align:start size:88% position:13%
we'll link to the
original interview below

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.665 align:start size:97% position:3%
if they want the full recap,
but can you just give me

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:20.967 align:start size:84% position:16%
a little of the Bryan
Dean Wright 101,

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:22.468
a little bit of your
history in the CIA?

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.737 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then also we have a sort
of similar political path

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.306
that we should get
into a bit as well.

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:30.009 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You bet, yeah, so I began
my career with the CIA

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.778
just after the 9/11 attacks.

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:34.347
It was October of 2001.

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:36.115
You know, we were all panicked

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:38.818
as we all started
our young careers.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.853
As folks who love this country,

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.488
we had just been
hit in the face.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.524
Nobody quite knew
exactly who, when,

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:48.094
and where abroad that we
might be hit from next.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:50.530
So that really kicked off
my career at the agency,

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.498
and I was there for a
good number of years

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:55.702 align:start position:0%
focused on weapons of mass
destruction, counter-terrorism.

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:59.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
As most of us did, focused
a little bit in Asia.

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:01.608 align:start size:97% position:3%
I can't get in particulars,
and then also in Africa

00:04:01.608 --> 00:04:04.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was an amazing
career and I had a great,

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:06.879
great time doing it
and been fortunate

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:08.681
to actually teach the next cadre

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:11.117
or next generation
of officers as well.

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:13.019
So I've had a really,
really fun career.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:15.955 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then towards the
very end, got introduced

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:18.424
to a few different
people to include you

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:19.826
and had a great opportunity

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:22.262 align:start size:97% position:3%
that was just by lucky
happenstance to start talking

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:24.163 align:start size:84% position:16%
about different
issues in the world,

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.798
particularly national security.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:29.769 align:start size:97% position:3%
And here we are with a podcast
and I'm really excited.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:32.372
- How tough is it to
make that transition?

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:35.375
Because CIA, you
gotta be somebody

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:37.610
that can't drop all the
secrets all the time.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:38.811
And then next thing you know,

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:41.347 align:start size:88% position:13%
you're talking on
camera, doing a podcast.

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:42.615
- Yeah.

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.083
- How do you blend
those two things?

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:46.786
- Spend 20 years avoiding
cameras and attention.

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:50.523 align:start size:88% position:13%
And now here I am,
it's an odd transition.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:51.858
You know, I think if
you talk to anybody

00:04:51.858 --> 00:04:54.093
who has really been
a true operator,

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:56.863 align:start size:97% position:3%
they understand the
importance of being anonymous.

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:58.865 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, unlike,
let's say, a James Bond

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:02.068
or those characters, the idea
isn't you go into somewhere

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:04.404
and you start blowing stuff up.

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:06.272 align:start size:84% position:16%
The idea is you go
in, you're very quiet.

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:08.207
You're discreet. You
do what you need to do.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:10.543 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then you leave and
actually no one ever knows.

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:13.546
So if you're pointing out
a gun or tossing a bomb,

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:15.615 align:start size:84% position:16%
something's gone
pretty wrong, right?

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:19.285 align:start size:97% position:3%
But the idea of then
sitting in front of a camera

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:21.921 align:start size:88% position:13%
and engaging people
yes, was absolutely odd.

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:24.590
But I will tell you
that in many ways,

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:29.529 align:start size:97% position:3%
the job has a lot of parallels
in that if you do it well,

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:32.031
and if you do it right,
and with all, truly,

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:33.499
I think you're one of them.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:36.669
You really can capture
people's hearts and minds

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.171
and you can move people.

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.706
And I think with intelligence,

00:05:39.706 --> 00:05:43.176
you can do that with your
listeners or your viewers,

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:44.777 align:start size:97% position:3%
that you know, if you're
briefing the President, right,

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:47.413
so the president's daily
brief is an actual brief

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.882
given to the President of the
United States every morning

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.417
by our spies and analysts.

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:53.353
And you can capture the
President's attention,

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:55.688
not only with what's
happening in the world,

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:58.024
but how do we solve the problems

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:00.660
and why he or she should
care about those problems.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:03.663
So I think in that sense,
there are some parallels,

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:07.367 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I'm really excited to
bring that kind of background

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:10.837
to this podcast and bring
listeners that same focus,

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:14.407
that same piece of critical
information every morning.

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:17.243 align:start position:0%
- So I actually wanna talk
about the real president's brief

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:20.680
that you just mentioned as
well as whether you think Joe

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:21.881
is actually reading it,

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:24.117 align:start size:88% position:13%
or whether they even
bother handing it to him

00:06:24.117 --> 00:06:25.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
or even if they're
printing it at this point.

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:27.820
But putting that
aside for a second,

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:31.424
it struck me as you were saying
that that if five years ago,

00:06:31.424 --> 00:06:33.659 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I had you on probably
maybe three or four years ago,

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:36.095 align:start size:88% position:13%
but if let's say five
or even seven years ago,

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:40.800
I had had a former CIA officer
on, my feeling about the CIA

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.770 align:start size:88% position:13%
as an institution
would be very different

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.506 align:start position:0%
than it is right now, and I
think a lot of people feel that.

00:06:46.506 --> 00:06:48.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's not with any
great pleasure I say that.

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:51.043
I suspect for you with
a lot of displeasure.

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:52.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah.
- Can you talk about what

00:06:52.245 --> 00:06:54.480 align:start size:84% position:16%
has sort of happened
to the agencies?

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:58.651 align:start position:0%
Like we see this woke thing
infecting absolutely everything.

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:01.220
I mean, the CIA, the
FBI, the military,

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:02.955
they're tweeting
about woke stuff

00:07:02.955 --> 00:07:05.191
more than seemingly doing

00:07:05.191 --> 00:07:07.693 align:start size:88% position:13%
whatever it is that
they are supposed to do,

00:07:07.693 --> 00:07:09.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
even if we're not supposed
to know all that stuff.

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:12.965
- Right, so, man, I'll tell
you that there are two things

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:15.902
that I think folks should
really be focusing on.

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:18.371
The first is the weaponization

00:07:18.371 --> 00:07:20.072
of the intelligence community.

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:23.476
You know, we knew back in
May of 2017 James Comey,

00:07:23.476 --> 00:07:25.445
the FBI director at the time

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:27.880
acknowledged that he
had leaked sensitive,

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:31.150 align:start size:97% position:3%
classified information to a
cutout to "The New York Times"

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:36.155 align:start position:0%
with the only goal of basically
hammering Donald Trump,

00:07:37.023 --> 00:07:38.491
getting a new special counsel

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:41.494
to investigate the Russia
collusion allegations.

00:07:41.494 --> 00:07:43.396
Now, Comey knew back then,

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:45.198
and unfortunately we
were only learning

00:07:45.198 --> 00:07:48.034
in the last number of years
that that was garbage, right?

00:07:48.034 --> 00:07:49.702
So we saw that in the FBI.

00:07:49.702 --> 00:07:52.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
We later saw it with a
guy named Kevin Clinesmith

00:07:52.338 --> 00:07:54.707
who was this very
senior FBI official

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:58.578
who'd falsified evidence to
a court to get surveillance

00:07:58.578 --> 00:08:01.347 align:start size:88% position:13%
or continue surveillance
on Carter Page.

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:04.417 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I think that had you
told me that seven years ago

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:06.953
that that was in the realm
of possible, I would've,

00:08:06.953 --> 00:08:09.088 align:start size:84% position:16%
to be honest with you,
I would've laughed
you outta the room

00:08:09.088 --> 00:08:12.391
because what I knew to be
true is that we had people

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:14.560
who were committed
to the rule of law,

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:16.062
whether it be the
FBI or the CIA.

00:08:16.062 --> 00:08:19.165
We were committed to our
oaths to be non-political,

00:08:19.165 --> 00:08:21.234 align:start size:84% position:16%
apolitical, certainly
when we walked

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:24.237
through those front doors and
we were focused on mission,

00:08:24.237 --> 00:08:27.940 align:start size:97% position:3%
but that has been completely
and utterly annihilated.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:31.210 align:start size:97% position:3%
That is to say, my belief that
the intelligence community

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:33.880
and the FBI are not
political, they are.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:35.681
We have proof. We have evidence.

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:38.985 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's painful because at the
very moment that we are facing

00:08:38.985 --> 00:08:40.853 align:start size:84% position:16%
this massive
challenge with China,

00:08:40.853 --> 00:08:44.690
this huge issue with Russia,
we actually need a really good,

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:46.692 align:start size:84% position:16%
healthy, functional
intelligence community

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:48.294
and law enforcement community.

00:08:48.294 --> 00:08:50.863
And on the federal level,
we just, we don't have it.

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:53.799
I can't tell you or
the folks watching

00:08:53.799 --> 00:08:56.502
that they've got the kind of
government that they deserve

00:08:56.502 --> 00:08:58.404 align:start size:84% position:16%
because I don't
think that they do.

00:08:58.404 --> 00:09:01.140
- Do you know when
that started there?

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.142 align:start size:88% position:13%
'Cause now we're seeing
it more obviously,

00:09:03.142 --> 00:09:05.745 align:start size:97% position:3%
but it didn't just start
because they started tweeting

00:09:05.745 --> 00:09:08.314
about this stuff six
months ago, obviously.

00:09:08.314 --> 00:09:11.517
- Yeah, well, I'll tell
you, I think candidly,

00:09:11.517 --> 00:09:13.719
politics aside, I think
during the Obama years,

00:09:13.719 --> 00:09:17.290
you started seeing a lot
of people misunderstanding

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:21.294
that they were there to be
of service to their country.

00:09:21.294 --> 00:09:23.996
And instead those agencies
and ultimately their country

00:09:23.996 --> 00:09:25.765
is supposed to be
of service to them.

00:09:25.765 --> 00:09:29.101
I mean, Jack Kennedy said it
very famously many decades ago.

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:31.604 align:start size:88% position:13%
That started to change,
I think, culturally

00:09:31.604 --> 00:09:34.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the Obama years because
it was really about me.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:38.344
It was about the self, my
truth and celebrating that.

00:09:38.344 --> 00:09:42.048
And so we went, I think,
from in the early 2000s

00:09:42.048 --> 00:09:44.650 align:start size:84% position:16%
when people were
saying very clearly,

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.752
"Look, it doesn't matter
if you're gay or straight

00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:48.354 align:start size:84% position:16%
or Christian or Muslim
or Black and White.

00:09:48.354 --> 00:09:49.689
Just come in and be of service.

00:09:49.689 --> 00:09:51.424 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
Leave your politics
at the door."

00:09:51.424 --> 00:09:54.160 align:start position:0% line:0%
So that was, I think, where
most of us would be, is to say,

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.529 align:start position:0% line:0%
yeah, get the equal opportunity
that's focused on mission.

00:09:56.529 --> 00:09:59.198
And now it's become,
instead of mission

00:09:59.198 --> 00:10:01.834 align:start size:84% position:16%
or really at the same
level of mission,

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:03.269
tell me what you're
passionate about,

00:10:03.269 --> 00:10:04.470
what your interests are.

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:06.739
Like, tell me your
story and your truth,

00:10:06.739 --> 00:10:09.041 align:start size:84% position:16%
the stuff that's not
mission critical,

00:10:09.041 --> 00:10:10.242
but it's being treated as such.

00:10:10.242 --> 00:10:12.411 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I can tell a couple
of amazing stories

00:10:12.411 --> 00:10:13.913
on the inside of the agency

00:10:13.913 --> 00:10:18.117
about how the racial woke
piece is really detrimental

00:10:18.117 --> 00:10:20.519 align:start size:88% position:13%
or playing a profoundly
detrimental role

00:10:20.519 --> 00:10:22.521
in mission criticalness.

00:10:22.521 --> 00:10:23.823
- Give me one of those.

00:10:23.823 --> 00:10:25.591 align:start size:88% position:13%
- All right, so there
was an individual whose-

00:10:25.591 --> 00:10:26.892
- Pick one, any one.

00:10:26.892 --> 00:10:28.594
- Yeah, a lot of
'em, unfortunately.

00:10:28.594 --> 00:10:31.097
There was a Black officer

00:10:31.097 --> 00:10:33.065
who wanted to start
an organization,

00:10:33.065 --> 00:10:36.936
an internal organization
where only Black people,

00:10:36.936 --> 00:10:41.007 align:start position:0%
and then he would have
preferred only Black gay people

00:10:41.007 --> 00:10:42.608
could come to a meeting, right.

00:10:42.608 --> 00:10:46.178 align:start position:0%
So in other words, on government
property inside Langley

00:10:46.178 --> 00:10:47.880
you had to be Black
and you had to be gay

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:49.849
in order to come
to those meetings.

00:10:49.849 --> 00:10:51.584 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now, I don't even
know how many people

00:10:51.584 --> 00:10:53.753 align:start size:97% position:3%
would even fit the bill there,
maybe like seven or eight

00:10:53.753 --> 00:10:55.187 align:start size:97% position:3%
so I'm not sure what you
would've done at that meeting,

00:10:55.187 --> 00:10:57.223
but nevertheless, the point is

00:10:57.223 --> 00:11:00.559 align:start size:97% position:3%
there was this very clearly
discriminatory request

00:11:00.559 --> 00:11:02.495 align:start size:88% position:13%
by an officer who should
have known better,

00:11:02.495 --> 00:11:05.431
but he made the request and
the Office of General Counsel

00:11:05.431 --> 00:11:08.100
had to come in and say, "No,
that is wildly inappropriate.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.035
We're not doing that."

00:11:09.035 --> 00:11:11.103
And he was actually livid.

00:11:11.103 --> 00:11:13.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, he was livid
that he had to be told no

00:11:13.939 --> 00:11:15.841
and to be reminded of the law.

00:11:15.841 --> 00:11:19.178 align:start size:97% position:3%
So that kind of wokeism
stuff matched with, I think,

00:11:19.178 --> 00:11:20.980
some of the PR stuff you see

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:22.782
coming out of the
CIA these days.

00:11:22.782 --> 00:11:25.451 align:start position:0%
You may recall that young woman
in the Twitter video saying

00:11:25.451 --> 00:11:28.387
that she was a, what was this?

00:11:28.387 --> 00:11:32.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it bisexual or lesbian
Latina who has ADHD-

00:11:32.391 --> 00:11:33.626
- Oh, yeah, yeah. She had
a little of everything.

00:11:33.626 --> 00:11:36.362 align:start size:84% position:16%
- She went through the
woke Olympics list.

00:11:36.362 --> 00:11:38.064
So that, I'm sorry to say

00:11:38.064 --> 00:11:40.132 align:start size:84% position:16%
has really become
the younger culture.

00:11:40.132 --> 00:11:42.134
And, you know, folks who
are a little bit older

00:11:42.134 --> 00:11:44.837 align:start size:97% position:3%
who came through, I think
the era, frankly, of the '90s

00:11:44.837 --> 00:11:47.573
such as yourself and myself,
that the Gen Xers, we're like,

00:11:47.573 --> 00:11:48.908
"Look, we don't
care who you are.

00:11:48.908 --> 00:11:50.176
Just come in and do the work.

00:11:50.176 --> 00:11:52.978 align:start size:84% position:16%
We want to treat
everybody with respect

00:11:52.978 --> 00:11:54.880
and equal opportunity."

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:58.918
But it's now like, you now
have to believe what I do.

00:11:58.918 --> 00:12:02.054 align:start position:0%
And if you don't, you're a
bigot or a racist or homophobic,

00:12:02.054 --> 00:12:03.556
et cetera, and that's new.

00:12:03.556 --> 00:12:06.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's only been in
the past five to 10 years,

00:12:06.092 --> 00:12:08.194 align:start size:84% position:16%
really started under
the Obama years.

00:12:08.194 --> 00:12:10.129 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Are you shocked
that the institutions

00:12:10.129 --> 00:12:12.031 align:start size:84% position:16%
didn't have better
defenses against this?

00:12:12.031 --> 00:12:13.733
I've asked this to many guests

00:12:13.733 --> 00:12:15.601
from many different disciplines,

00:12:15.601 --> 00:12:17.403
usually at the education
level that you'd think

00:12:17.403 --> 00:12:20.873
that some of the STEM subjects
would've had better defenses.

00:12:20.873 --> 00:12:22.475
People are like, all right,
yeah, of course, you know,

00:12:22.475 --> 00:12:26.045 align:start size:97% position:3%
lesbian dance theory was
gonna go down, but you know,

00:12:26.045 --> 00:12:29.582
math perhaps or biology,
that should have been okay,

00:12:29.582 --> 00:12:30.883 align:start size:84% position:16%
but now we're seeing
it across there.

00:12:30.883 --> 00:12:33.719 align:start size:84% position:16%
Are you surprised that
our actual, I mean,

00:12:33.719 --> 00:12:38.090
these are our most highest
elite security services now

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:39.592
are going down that
they did not have

00:12:39.592 --> 00:12:40.926
some fail safe in there?

00:12:41.827 --> 00:12:43.596
- Look, am I surprised? Yeah.

00:12:43.596 --> 00:12:45.765
I think most people in
this country right now

00:12:45.765 --> 00:12:47.666 align:start size:84% position:16%
are not just surprised
but shocked, right?

00:12:47.666 --> 00:12:49.769
I think most people
want to be reasonable

00:12:49.769 --> 00:12:51.337
and want to be compassionate

00:12:51.337 --> 00:12:54.607
about welcoming different
people into their families

00:12:54.607 --> 00:12:56.709
and to their communities.

00:12:56.709 --> 00:13:01.614
But we're seeing that go well
beyond any degree of reason.

00:13:02.748 --> 00:13:03.983 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so I think the
CIA, you're seeing it,

00:13:03.983 --> 00:13:05.518
a reflection of what
people are experiencing

00:13:05.518 --> 00:13:07.453
outside of Langley in
their own families,

00:13:07.453 --> 00:13:08.854
in their own communities.

00:13:08.854 --> 00:13:11.257 align:start size:97% position:3%
They're feeling that
pressure to sort of conform.

00:13:11.257 --> 00:13:13.292
And then they're being
told from the top down

00:13:13.292 --> 00:13:15.694
from the President's
office, him or herself,

00:13:15.694 --> 00:13:17.129
you have to do this.

00:13:17.129 --> 00:13:19.565
And they're like, well,
I'm not gonna be fired

00:13:19.565 --> 00:13:21.901 align:start size:84% position:16%
so I guess I have
to go along with it.

00:13:21.901 --> 00:13:23.903 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's what I
think you're seeing.

00:13:23.903 --> 00:13:27.039
Even the very, very smart,
very critical thinking people

00:13:27.039 --> 00:13:28.541 align:start size:84% position:16%
are starting to
fall into this trap

00:13:28.541 --> 00:13:30.910
because they're gonna lose
their job if they don't.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:34.947
- When you saw the
51, I believe it was,

00:13:34.947 --> 00:13:39.952
former intelligence
officers who all said

00:13:41.387 --> 00:13:43.522
that the Hunter Biden laptop
was Russian misinformation

00:13:43.522 --> 00:13:45.424
or disinformation,
they all said it

00:13:45.424 --> 00:13:47.960
without having seen it, okay?

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:49.228
When you saw that.

00:13:49.228 --> 00:13:52.264 align:start size:88% position:13%
So let's go back before
it's been debunked,

00:13:52.264 --> 00:13:53.666
but when it originally came out,

00:13:53.666 --> 00:13:55.067
I'm talking during the election,

00:13:55.067 --> 00:13:56.669
when they all came
out and said that,

00:13:56.669 --> 00:13:58.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
conveniently enough,
right before the election.

00:13:58.671 --> 00:14:01.941
What was your take
then compared to now?

00:14:03.342 --> 00:14:06.679 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Hmm, hmm, both then and
now my reaction was the same.

00:14:06.679 --> 00:14:08.581 align:start size:84% position:16%
There is absolutely
no way to know

00:14:08.581 --> 00:14:10.216
unless you do a
forensic analysis

00:14:10.216 --> 00:14:12.785 align:start size:97% position:3%
of whether or not that laptop,
A, belonged to Hunter Biden

00:14:12.785 --> 00:14:15.988 align:start size:97% position:3%
and B, if there was any
additional information added

00:14:15.988 --> 00:14:18.390 align:start size:97% position:3%
that would be thus
disinformation or propaganda

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:21.093 align:start size:97% position:3%
or part of some sort of covert
action op by the Russians,

00:14:21.093 --> 00:14:23.195 align:start size:84% position:16%
the Chinese,
whoever it might be.

00:14:23.195 --> 00:14:27.633 align:start size:97% position:3%
So to immediately come out and
just dismiss it was absurd.

00:14:27.633 --> 00:14:29.134
And what it showed me

00:14:29.134 --> 00:14:32.304
was that those people on
that list were partisans.

00:14:32.304 --> 00:14:36.942
They were using the stink, as
it were, of working at the CIA

00:14:36.942 --> 00:14:39.545 align:start size:84% position:16%
being an intelligence
officer to go out

00:14:39.545 --> 00:14:42.648
to the American people with
some degree of gravitas,

00:14:42.648 --> 00:14:45.751 align:start position:0%
like they're sort of mini James
Bond or whoever it might be

00:14:45.751 --> 00:14:47.987
and so you're gonna
take them seriously.

00:14:47.987 --> 00:14:52.358
And so they abused their
professional histories

00:14:52.358 --> 00:14:54.393
to make this partisan point.

00:14:54.393 --> 00:14:56.328 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so again, we
saw this by the way,

00:14:56.328 --> 00:14:59.498 align:start size:84% position:16%
not just with the
Hunter Biden laptop.

00:14:59.498 --> 00:15:01.734
We saw this with
the Steele dossier.

00:15:01.734 --> 00:15:05.604 align:start size:97% position:3%
That's perhaps even more
egregious years prior to that,

00:15:05.604 --> 00:15:08.207
when I think you could
say, where's a point

00:15:08.207 --> 00:15:10.142
where we really started
seeing this publicly.

00:15:10.142 --> 00:15:12.177
You had a whole bunch of
intelligence officials

00:15:12.177 --> 00:15:15.381 align:start size:97% position:3%
who damn well know better
that when you get information

00:15:15.381 --> 00:15:17.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was what was
inside the Steele dossier

00:15:17.216 --> 00:15:18.484
which is from Russia, right,

00:15:18.484 --> 00:15:22.221
that you had to tread
very, very cautiously

00:15:22.221 --> 00:15:25.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
around Russian intel
because of the likelihood

00:15:25.024 --> 00:15:27.092
that it has been
fed, in this case,

00:15:27.092 --> 00:15:29.895
to Steele, the British spy.

00:15:29.895 --> 00:15:31.563
So when you had people saying,

00:15:31.563 --> 00:15:34.166
"Oh, the Steele dossier is
true, it's gotta be true."

00:15:34.166 --> 00:15:35.434
That's when I was like,

00:15:35.434 --> 00:15:37.937
all right, this whole
thing has been cooked.

00:15:37.937 --> 00:15:42.041
This is absolutely
members of the IC

00:15:42.041 --> 00:15:45.477 align:start size:97% position:3%
wanting to be part of the
Hillary Clinton administration

00:15:45.477 --> 00:15:47.346
or the Joe Biden
administration now

00:15:47.346 --> 00:15:49.081
who are trying to gain favor

00:15:49.081 --> 00:15:51.317
and they're using their
backgrounds to do so.

00:15:51.317 --> 00:15:54.887 align:start position:0%
And it's just infuriating
because ultimately what happens

00:15:54.887 --> 00:15:59.058
and what has happened is that
the American people lose faith

00:15:59.058 --> 00:16:00.592
in the intelligence community.

00:16:00.592 --> 00:16:03.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
They lose faith in the
law enforcement community.

00:16:03.495 --> 00:16:05.064
And rightfully so.

00:16:05.064 --> 00:16:07.199 align:start position:0%
And so when that happens, you've
got a whole bunch of people

00:16:07.199 --> 00:16:09.034
with lots of profound powers

00:16:09.034 --> 00:16:11.437
who don't actually have the
support of American people.

00:16:11.437 --> 00:16:15.507 align:start position:0%
They start acting basically
with impunity because they can.

00:16:15.507 --> 00:16:19.211 align:start size:97% position:3%
Countries start falling apart
when this stuff happens.

00:16:19.211 --> 00:16:22.581 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that's the part that
I'm so profoundly afraid of.

00:16:22.581 --> 00:16:26.318
- Right, so I try not to be a
crazy alarmist on this show.

00:16:26.318 --> 00:16:29.054 align:start size:88% position:13%
Try, maybe I fail at
it, but I try not to be,

00:16:29.054 --> 00:16:31.323
but it seems to me that's
kind of where we're at

00:16:31.323 --> 00:16:35.995 align:start size:84% position:16%
because when the 51
intelligence officers,

00:16:37.629 --> 00:16:38.998
in essence, former-
- Propagandists.

00:16:38.998 --> 00:16:40.833 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Propagandists. I
was trying to be nice.

00:16:40.833 --> 00:16:42.434 align:start size:84% position:16%
Thank you for cleaning
that up for me.

00:16:42.434 --> 00:16:44.169 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, you don't have-
- When those 51 propagandists

00:16:44.169 --> 00:16:47.573 align:start size:97% position:3%
were exposed as such,
meaning "The New York Times"

00:16:47.573 --> 00:16:50.576 align:start position:0%
finally a year and a half
later, everyone knows this now,

00:16:50.576 --> 00:16:52.544 align:start size:84% position:16%
a month and a half ago
or so finally said,

00:16:52.544 --> 00:16:54.713
"Yeah, yeah, the laptop
was real, by the way."

00:16:54.713 --> 00:16:56.382 align:start size:84% position:16%
Did anyone get called
into an office?

00:16:56.382 --> 00:16:58.784
Did anyone get fired from
a consulting gig they got?

00:16:58.784 --> 00:17:00.753
Did anyone get fired from a
lobbying firm or anything?

00:17:00.753 --> 00:17:04.823
I suspect not, and that goes
to your point about the trust.

00:17:04.823 --> 00:17:06.859
It's like, I think
they sort of feel

00:17:06.859 --> 00:17:08.127
like can get away with anything

00:17:08.127 --> 00:17:10.562
'cause they can get
away with anything.

00:17:10.562 --> 00:17:14.466
- Yeah, well, and there was
a report out sometime back

00:17:14.466 --> 00:17:17.736
that the Joe Biden
administration has
actually encouraged

00:17:17.736 --> 00:17:21.640 align:start size:97% position:3%
and allowed this junk intel
to go out about Ukraine

00:17:23.108 --> 00:17:26.578
all because he wants to try to
encourage the American people

00:17:26.578 --> 00:17:29.715
to embrace a greater
involvement in the war.

00:17:29.715 --> 00:17:34.486 align:start size:84% position:16%
So you are having
this intelligence
fiasco after fiasco.

00:17:34.486 --> 00:17:36.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
And at some level, I
think a reasonable person

00:17:36.555 --> 00:17:38.057
says, "I've had enough.

00:17:38.057 --> 00:17:40.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
Whenever you say 'American
intelligence assesses,'

00:17:40.859 --> 00:17:42.061
I'm not gonna believe it."

00:17:42.061 --> 00:17:43.929 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I can't tell those
people right now,

00:17:43.929 --> 00:17:46.799
particularly with the current
leadership that they're wrong.

00:17:46.799 --> 00:17:51.236 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that's really sad for a
guy who spent most of his life

00:17:51.236 --> 00:17:52.237
in the world of intelligence.

00:17:52.237 --> 00:17:53.405
- Let's shift that a little bit

00:17:53.405 --> 00:17:54.673
to what you just
mentioned there.

00:17:54.673 --> 00:17:56.608 align:start size:84% position:16%
So this Russia-Ukraine
situation,

00:17:56.608 --> 00:17:59.545 align:start size:97% position:3%
I actually have not covered
it a ton on the show.

00:17:59.545 --> 00:18:01.814 align:start size:97% position:3%
I was very honest with my
audience from the beginning.

00:18:01.814 --> 00:18:06.819
I was kind of like, this whole
thing reads very weird to me,

00:18:08.187 --> 00:18:11.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
the whole setup, the
Biden laptop piece of it.

00:18:11.423 --> 00:18:14.560 align:start size:84% position:16%
Suddenly we all gotta
hate Russia. I'm not
defending Russia.

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:16.195
You can't just invade
a sovereign nation,

00:18:16.195 --> 00:18:19.865
but it just felt like
so much propaganda

00:18:19.865 --> 00:18:21.834 align:start size:88% position:13%
that I've bounced
around it a little bit.

00:18:21.834 --> 00:18:23.535 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I've talked about
the after-affects

00:18:23.535 --> 00:18:26.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
meaning inflation and
gas and things like that.

00:18:26.238 --> 00:18:27.473
And I've tried to talk

00:18:27.473 --> 00:18:29.775
about what we should do
perhaps and should do,

00:18:29.775 --> 00:18:33.078 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I'm not doing the daily
thing with Russia and Ukraine.

00:18:33.078 --> 00:18:37.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you able to assess
information properly?

00:18:37.316 --> 00:18:39.084 align:start size:84% position:16%
Because I think people
are just, you know,

00:18:39.084 --> 00:18:41.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
you put the Ukrainian flag
in your Twitter avatar.

00:18:41.420 --> 00:18:44.189
Everybody else is an
evil Nazi, that's it.

00:18:44.189 --> 00:18:46.592
I suspect it's not
quite that simple.

00:18:46.592 --> 00:18:48.694
- Oh dear. No.

00:18:48.694 --> 00:18:51.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you know that you're
caught in a hysteria when,

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:54.800
and this is true, both
of the major marathons

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:58.804 align:start position:0%
in this country have banned
runners from Ukraine or Russia,

00:18:58.804 --> 00:19:02.341 align:start position:0%
or I should say Russia or
Belorussia from running, right?

00:19:02.341 --> 00:19:03.542
So we're banning
marathon runners-

00:19:03.542 --> 00:19:04.943 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, not Ukraine,
not Ukraine.

00:19:04.943 --> 00:19:06.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Because of their
national identity, right?

00:19:06.178 --> 00:19:07.613
And we're pouring out, you know,

00:19:07.613 --> 00:19:10.849 align:start size:97% position:3%
we're renaming chicken
Kiev and it's chicken Kyiv.

00:19:10.849 --> 00:19:15.187
Stop, all right. This
is hysteria defined.

00:19:15.187 --> 00:19:19.358 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I think that it's important
for people like me to speak

00:19:19.358 --> 00:19:21.760 align:start size:84% position:16%
to these issues
around war and peace

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:23.295
and including in Ukraine

00:19:23.295 --> 00:19:25.831
knowing that there is
a fog of war issue.

00:19:25.831 --> 00:19:28.600 align:start size:97% position:3%
So when I talk about
Ukraine or any other places

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:31.670
