Nancy Pelosi's been there 87
years, something like that.

00:38:45.523 --> 00:38:47.825 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah.
- It's just, it never ends.

00:38:47.825 --> 00:38:49.927
Can you talk a little
bit about generally

00:38:49.927 --> 00:38:54.932 align:start size:88% position:13%
how in politics
secrets remain secrets?

00:38:56.300 --> 00:38:59.170 align:start size:97% position:3%
Or things like, for example,
things that we can see

00:38:59.170 --> 00:39:01.172
that we all can kind of
see with our own eyes

00:39:01.172 --> 00:39:03.040 align:start size:84% position:16%
that somehow just
never get discussed.

00:39:03.040 --> 00:39:06.510
So the Biden cognitive
stuff, it's obvious.

00:39:06.510 --> 00:39:07.912
Everyone knows it.

00:39:07.912 --> 00:39:10.948 align:start size:84% position:16%
Every single person
that you mentioned to,

00:39:10.948 --> 00:39:12.316
you talk about it privately,

00:39:12.316 --> 00:39:14.752 align:start size:97% position:3%
everyone will admit
something is not right there,

00:39:14.752 --> 00:39:16.921 align:start size:97% position:3%
but no one's allowed to
talk about it on mainstream.

00:39:16.921 --> 00:39:18.322
It's never brought up.

00:39:18.322 --> 00:39:20.725 align:start position:0%
Meanwhile, if Trump was
slurring every one of his words

00:39:20.725 --> 00:39:24.595
and making up stories
and having these blips

00:39:24.595 --> 00:39:27.031
that just go completely awry,

00:39:27.031 --> 00:39:31.202 align:start size:97% position:3%
we woulda 25th Amendment-ed
him seven times ago.

00:39:31.202 --> 00:39:33.571 align:start size:81% position:19%
So what do we do?
- Yeah.

00:39:33.571 --> 00:39:35.473
- How does that happen,
I guess is the question.

00:39:35.473 --> 00:39:36.807
- Well, I think we-
- Not what do we do.

00:39:36.807 --> 00:39:39.076
I have some ideas.
I just said of them,

00:39:39.076 --> 00:39:41.212
25th Amendment.
- Yeah. (laughs).

00:39:41.212 --> 00:39:42.947
Look, I think you can look
back in American history.

00:39:42.947 --> 00:39:45.549
There have been times when
the media has stepped in

00:39:45.549 --> 00:39:47.785 align:start size:84% position:16%
to hide a deficiency
of a leader.

00:39:47.785 --> 00:39:49.453
So I'm thinking of Roosevelt

00:39:49.453 --> 00:39:51.622 align:start size:84% position:16%
and some of his
physical challenges

00:39:51.622 --> 00:39:53.224 align:start size:84% position:16%
being in a wheelchair
and so forth

00:39:53.224 --> 00:39:54.759
so it's not unprecedented.

00:39:54.759 --> 00:39:57.194
The issue is, why are we hiding?

00:39:57.194 --> 00:39:59.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is to say, why is the
press hiding this thing

00:39:59.663 --> 00:40:01.332
that might otherwise be bad

00:40:01.332 --> 00:40:03.067
or perceived as
bad in the world?

00:40:03.067 --> 00:40:06.837
You know, for Roosevelt,
it was about, you know,

00:40:06.837 --> 00:40:08.973
would people view him as weak

00:40:08.973 --> 00:40:12.042
if he couldn't stand up on
his own two feet, right?

00:40:12.042 --> 00:40:15.045
But otherwise his mind, his
decision-making processes,

00:40:15.045 --> 00:40:18.015
the ability to surround
himself with smart people

00:40:18.015 --> 00:40:19.884 align:start size:88% position:13%
and make good decisions
for the country,

00:40:19.884 --> 00:40:21.385
that was never in doubt.

00:40:21.385 --> 00:40:25.823
So it was more of a, this is
a private matter that made him

00:40:25.823 --> 00:40:28.959
sort of look less manly perhaps.

00:40:28.959 --> 00:40:30.127
It was wrong, of course.

00:40:30.127 --> 00:40:31.562 align:start size:84% position:16%
He was just as
manly as he was ever

00:40:31.562 --> 00:40:33.130 line:0%
in a wheelchair or otherwise,

00:40:33.130 --> 00:40:35.433 line:0%
but at the time that
was kind of the logic.

00:40:35.433 --> 00:40:37.935 line:0%
It was a bit more of
a genteel approach

00:40:37.935 --> 00:40:40.237 line:0%
to a personal problem, right?

00:40:40.237 --> 00:40:41.872
But that's not the case anymore.

00:40:41.872 --> 00:40:44.775
The press is basically
serving as the mouthpiece

00:40:44.775 --> 00:40:46.944 align:start size:84% position:16%
for different
politicians, right?

00:40:46.944 --> 00:40:49.947
So it's, I don't want
this embarrassing thing

00:40:49.947 --> 00:40:54.018
about their infidelity or
their cognitive impairment

00:40:54.018 --> 00:40:55.686
or the fact that
they've taken on

00:40:55.686 --> 00:40:57.221
whatever degree of
corruption, right?

00:40:57.221 --> 00:40:59.790
Their insider trading
with stocks, et cetera.

00:40:59.790 --> 00:41:01.926
So now the press
knows those things.

00:41:01.926 --> 00:41:05.996 align:start size:97% position:3%
And if the person who's
created or engaged in the sin,

00:41:05.996 --> 00:41:07.531
for lack of a better word,

00:41:07.531 --> 00:41:10.801
I'm gonna hide it because
they're on my team, right?

00:41:10.801 --> 00:41:13.137 align:start size:84% position:16%
So the press has
become part of a team.

00:41:13.137 --> 00:41:14.939
And when you have that,

00:41:14.939 --> 00:41:16.774
and the data, by the
way, supports that,

00:41:16.774 --> 00:41:19.076 align:start size:88% position:13%
we know that for
instance, that the press

00:41:19.076 --> 00:41:21.345
gives overwhelmingly
to Democrats anywhere,

00:41:21.345 --> 00:41:26.350
depending on the poll you
look at 83, 85% to 95 98%,

00:41:27.485 --> 00:41:28.285 align:start size:88% position:13%
no matter where you
look, it's overwhelming.

00:41:28.285 --> 00:41:29.787
- [Dave] Yeah, yeah.

00:41:29.787 --> 00:41:31.689
- So they've chosen a team
and are hiding the bad stuff

00:41:31.689 --> 00:41:33.190
that their team engages in.

00:41:33.190 --> 00:41:34.959
That's what's different

00:41:34.959 --> 00:41:37.094
as compared to what's
happened historically.

00:41:37.094 --> 00:41:38.462
So how do you change that.

00:41:38.462 --> 00:41:40.464
You just keep calling it about,

00:41:40.464 --> 00:41:42.433
and the American people see it.

00:41:42.433 --> 00:41:44.668 align:start size:97% position:3%
And what's happening is
they're starting to gravitate

00:41:44.668 --> 00:41:47.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
to voices that they think
are more reasonable.

00:41:47.104 --> 00:41:49.006 align:start size:84% position:16%
So mainstream media's
being challenged

00:41:49.006 --> 00:41:51.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
by sort of smaller
voices, but that's great.

00:41:51.709 --> 00:41:53.277
It's a marketplace of ideas.

00:41:53.277 --> 00:41:56.180 align:start size:97% position:3%
It allows really, really smart
people, yourself and others

00:41:56.180 --> 00:41:59.817 align:start position:0%
to stand up and say, "Hey, look,
listen, here's my own bias.

00:41:59.817 --> 00:42:01.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna admit it,
unlike some of the people

00:42:01.886 --> 00:42:04.455 align:start size:97% position:3%
in mainstream media, I'm gonna
tell you what my biases are

00:42:04.455 --> 00:42:07.558
and where I've come from as
Bryan as a former Democrat,

00:42:07.558 --> 00:42:09.226
now Republican conservative.

00:42:09.226 --> 00:42:10.761 align:start size:81% position:19%
Like, you know
that on the table.

00:42:10.761 --> 00:42:12.096
I'm not hiding any of that.

00:42:12.096 --> 00:42:13.531 align:start size:84% position:16%
So let me present
to you the material.

00:42:13.531 --> 00:42:15.266 align:start size:81% position:19%
I'm gonna offer
you my reflection.

00:42:15.266 --> 00:42:16.400 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then you can decide
what to do with it

00:42:16.400 --> 00:42:18.369
or add it to other voices."

00:42:18.369 --> 00:42:20.838
I think that's what's going
to just naturally happen

00:42:20.838 --> 00:42:22.573
and is already happening.

00:42:22.573 --> 00:42:25.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Are there any countries
or security services,

00:42:25.776 --> 00:42:28.779
information services that are
doing it significantly better?

00:42:28.779 --> 00:42:30.681
Like if we get the
right people in,

00:42:30.681 --> 00:42:34.251
is there anyone we can look
at that is doing it right?

00:42:34.251 --> 00:42:35.719
And we could be like,

00:42:35.719 --> 00:42:38.789 align:start size:97% position:3%
"Hey, borrow the manual
that they have over there."

00:42:38.789 --> 00:42:42.526 align:start position:0%
- No, I'm sorry to say that
this issue of the politicization

00:42:42.526 --> 00:42:45.129
of media is widespread,
it's across the country.

00:42:45.129 --> 00:42:48.966
And it's been bad in lots
of places for a long time.

00:42:48.966 --> 00:42:51.201 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I don't think
anybody's got it right,

00:42:51.201 --> 00:42:54.071
anybody's doing it
well, unfortunately,

00:42:54.071 --> 00:42:55.773
so that means that
we have to come up

00:42:55.773 --> 00:42:57.441
with the set of solutions.

00:42:57.441 --> 00:42:59.043
And I think we're gonna
try different things here

00:42:59.043 --> 00:43:01.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
and something's gonna work
and some things won't,

00:43:01.378 --> 00:43:04.882
and that's all right, but I
think at the end of the day,

00:43:04.882 --> 00:43:08.385
my hope, and you hate
to base a plan on this,

00:43:08.385 --> 00:43:10.487
is that there are gonna be
enough people in journalism

00:43:10.487 --> 00:43:13.057
and the owners and the
editors who are like,

00:43:13.057 --> 00:43:15.659 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Look, we're losing
audience share,

00:43:15.659 --> 00:43:17.394
and they're going
to other places

00:43:17.394 --> 00:43:18.862
and listening to other people

00:43:19.997 --> 00:43:21.966 align:start size:84% position:16%
because we are such
partisan folks.

00:43:21.966 --> 00:43:25.603 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so we are incentivized,
advertisers like us

00:43:25.603 --> 00:43:27.237 align:start size:84% position:16%
because we've started
to gravitate back

00:43:27.237 --> 00:43:29.740 align:start size:84% position:16%
to just Cronkite-like
news, right?

00:43:30.941 --> 00:43:32.710
I would love to think
that that's possible.

00:43:32.710 --> 00:43:34.712 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't know that
it's gonna happen here

00:43:34.712 --> 00:43:38.916 align:start size:97% position:3%
because most of us click or
are attracted to media outlets

00:43:38.916 --> 00:43:41.518 align:start size:88% position:13%
and personalities who
reaffirm our own biases.

00:43:41.518 --> 00:43:44.088
So I don't know what's
gonna break that fever,

00:43:44.088 --> 00:43:45.522
but until it does-

00:43:45.522 --> 00:43:47.157
- What about on the
intelligence side?

00:43:47.157 --> 00:43:50.828 align:start position:0%
I'm with you on the media side,
but are there any countries

00:43:50.828 --> 00:43:53.364
here, this hemisphere,
the other hemisphere,

00:43:53.364 --> 00:43:54.565
maybe on another planet,

00:43:54.565 --> 00:43:56.767
is someone doing
this somewhat okay?

00:43:57.901 --> 00:43:59.403
- So I'll tell you,

00:43:59.403 --> 00:44:01.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that a lot of
that is pretty close hold

00:44:01.972 --> 00:44:04.642
so I don't know the extent to
which it's being rooted out.

00:44:04.642 --> 00:44:07.277 align:start size:84% position:16%
What I do know is that
in other countries,

00:44:07.277 --> 00:44:11.615
if they find that, there is
no real publicizing that.

00:44:11.615 --> 00:44:14.985 align:start size:97% position:3%
They end up just
disappearing people, right?

00:44:14.985 --> 00:44:16.787
They sort of clean
house in that sense.

00:44:16.787 --> 00:44:18.722
So unfortunately there is
no good path, but again,

00:44:18.722 --> 00:44:21.392
I would go back to the fact
what we did in the 1970s,

00:44:21.392 --> 00:44:25.763 align:start position:0%
when the CIA got so outta whack,
we dealt with it publicly,

00:44:25.763 --> 00:44:27.197
and then we had reforms.

00:44:27.197 --> 00:44:28.832
And so we did it before.

00:44:28.832 --> 00:44:31.268 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think we can do it
again with thoughtful people

00:44:31.268 --> 00:44:32.770
who understand that
the problem is real.

00:44:32.770 --> 00:44:34.405
That's the actual issue.

00:44:34.405 --> 00:44:35.739
Right now you have
people in Congress

00:44:35.739 --> 00:44:37.207 align:start size:81% position:19%
who don't think
the issue is real,

00:44:37.207 --> 00:44:39.643 align:start position:0%
that we don't have a politicized
intelligence community

00:44:39.643 --> 00:44:42.212
or a politicized law
enforcement community.

00:44:42.212 --> 00:44:43.814 align:start size:84% position:16%
Some of them believe
that privately,

00:44:43.814 --> 00:44:46.450
but they're not willing to
do anything about it publicly

00:44:46.450 --> 00:44:49.253 align:start size:97% position:3%
because the FBI or the CIA
has been on their side, right?

00:44:49.253 --> 00:44:50.921 align:start size:84% position:16%
You remember the
Democratic congressman

00:44:50.921 --> 00:44:54.425
who was gonna give a job to
the disgraced FBI official

00:44:54.425 --> 00:44:56.527 align:start size:84% position:16%
who'd done good things
for the Democrats.

00:44:56.527 --> 00:44:58.062
Like, that's the kind of stuff

00:44:58.062 --> 00:44:59.530 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you have to
remove those people,

00:44:59.530 --> 00:45:01.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
put in good people in
your House and your Senate

00:45:01.765 --> 00:45:03.267
who are focused on the country.

00:45:03.267 --> 00:45:05.703 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then you have these
panels, these investigations,

00:45:05.703 --> 00:45:07.671 align:start size:88% position:13%
you come up with reforms
and you get it done.

00:45:07.671 --> 00:45:09.807
We've done it before.
We can do it again.

00:45:09.807 --> 00:45:11.642
- Usually when they screw
up or lie to Congress,

00:45:11.642 --> 00:45:15.345 align:start size:97% position:3%
they just get a job on CNN.
- Right. (laughs)

00:45:16.747 --> 00:45:17.881
Touche, yeah.

00:45:17.881 --> 00:45:19.550
- That's generally how it works.

00:45:19.550 --> 00:45:23.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
Bryan, I suspect a
political future for you.

00:45:23.253 --> 00:45:25.689
I don't know that
you suspect one,

00:45:25.689 --> 00:45:27.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I thought you were
gonna make that very face,

00:45:27.591 --> 00:45:30.060
but I suspect one.

00:45:30.060 --> 00:45:32.396
- You know, well, okay,
look, that's very kind.

00:45:32.396 --> 00:45:35.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
Seriously, I mean, I go
back to this idea of like,

00:45:35.599 --> 00:45:38.268
it's our Republic,
if we can keep it.

00:45:38.268 --> 00:45:41.505 align:start position:0%
So as much as I make that
grimaced face, as everyone does,

00:45:41.505 --> 00:45:43.974 align:start size:97% position:3%
we have to all figure out
ways to get involved, right?

00:45:43.974 --> 00:45:46.677
So if that's running for
your local city council

00:45:46.677 --> 00:45:48.312
or being part of
your school board,

00:45:48.312 --> 00:45:50.881 align:start size:97% position:3%
if it's a county
commissioner at some level,

00:45:50.881 --> 00:45:54.118
it doesn't have to be
the top of the pole

00:45:54.118 --> 00:45:56.920
in terms of being President
or Senator or something.

00:45:56.920 --> 00:45:59.723
If that's your passion and
you've got the money, great.

00:45:59.723 --> 00:46:01.892 align:start size:84% position:16%
But just, we all
have to get involved.

00:46:01.892 --> 00:46:06.864
So my scrunchy face
getting involved

00:46:06.864 --> 00:46:09.433 align:start size:84% position:16%
is on the national
level, man, it's just,

00:46:09.433 --> 00:46:11.802 align:start position:0%
I think we all know what happens
when people run for office.

00:46:11.802 --> 00:46:16.206
Stuff gets yanked out of your
past completely misrepresented

00:46:17.374 --> 00:46:19.143 align:start size:84% position:16%
or, you know, you're
imperfect, right?

00:46:19.143 --> 00:46:20.778 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so nobody
wants to face that.

00:46:20.778 --> 00:46:23.147
I don't have a lot of that so
that's not what anchors me.

00:46:23.147 --> 00:46:26.483
It's just the idea of, man,
just being a public person,

00:46:26.483 --> 00:46:28.218
always under the microscope.

00:46:28.218 --> 00:46:29.486
So that's why I'm
doing a podcast

00:46:29.486 --> 00:46:31.088
so that doesn't make any sense.

00:46:31.088 --> 00:46:33.690
I love my argument. I'm just
undermined it, it's great.

00:46:33.690 --> 00:46:36.426 align:start position:0%
- Well, former County
Commissioner Bryan Dean Wright,

00:46:36.426 --> 00:46:38.529
I appreciate you doing the show

00:46:38.529 --> 00:46:40.764
and look forward
to seeing you soon.

00:46:40.764 --> 00:46:42.065
Thanks man.
- You betcha.

